  "problem": "In a particular school, $65%$ of students attend a literature course, and $45%$ of students attend a mathematics course. If $50%$ of mathematics students also attend a literature course, what is the probability that a randomly chosen literature student attends a mathematics course? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
